  "question": {
    "text": "If $y=\\frac{2 \\sin \\alpha}{1+\\cos \\alpha+\\sin \\alpha}$, then value of $\\frac{1-\\cos \\alpha+\\sin \\alpha}{1+\\sin \\alpha}$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{y}{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$y$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$2 y$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{2} y$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{1-\\cos \\alpha+\\sin \\alpha}{1+\\sin \\alpha}$\r\n\r\n$=\\frac{1-\\cos \\alpha+\\sin \\alpha}{1+\\sin \\alpha} \\cdot \\frac{1+\\cos \\alpha+\\sin \\alpha}{1+\\cos \\alpha+\\sin \\alpha}$\r\n\r\n$=\\frac{(1+\\sin \\alpha)^{2}-\\cos ^{2} \\alpha}{(1+\\sin \\alpha)(1+\\cos \\alpha+\\sin \\alpha)}$\r\n\r\n$=\\frac{\\left(1+\\sin ^{2} \\alpha+2 \\sin \\alpha\\right)-\\left(1-\\sin ^{2} \\alpha\\right)}{(1+\\sin \\alpha)(1+\\cos \\alpha+\\sin \\alpha)}$\r\n\r\n$=\\frac{2 \\sin \\alpha}{1+\\cos \\alpha+\\sin \\alpha}=y$"
  }
}